The function must handle edge cases: if the list is empty, return 0. If the target sum is negative or zero, the smallest subarray length is 0 because an empty subarray (if allowed) or a subarray with non-positive sum might qualify, but the problem expects only non-empty subarrays, so return 0 if no valid subarray exists. The algorithm should have linear time complexity with respect to the list length.

